.el .ds Aq '
.TH rars-test 1 "" rars
.SH NAME
rars\-test \- Verify archive integrity by extracting to a sink
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrars test\fR [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-password\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-legacy\-name\-encoding\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-buffered\-decode\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-decode\-workers\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-dictionary\-size\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-member\-output\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-total\-output\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-reader\-workspace\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-header\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-header\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-scratch\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-scratch\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-rar50\-filter\-memory\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-rar3\-vm\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIARCHIVE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verify archive integrity by extracting to a sink
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fI<PASSWORD>\fR
Archive password (visible in process list \[u2014] prefer \-\-password\-file or the TTY prompt)
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads for parallel compression and extraction (default: all available cores)
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read password from file ("\-" for stdin); trailing newlines are stripped
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
Progress reporting mode for long\-running operations
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-legacy\-name\-encoding\fR \fI<ENCODING>\fR
Source encoding for legacy names without Unicode (e.g. cp850 or detect)
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-buffered\-decode\-limit\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum RAR 5 member size to decode in memory; larger ones stream (default 16m)
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-decode\-workers\fR \fI<N>\fR
Threads decoding RAR5/7 blocks ahead of the output; 0 decodes serially (default: up to 8)
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-dictionary\-size\-limit\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum declared RAR5/7 dictionary size (not total memory)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-member\-output\-bytes\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum decoded output per logical member or archive comment
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-total\-output\-bytes\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum decoded output per extraction/test call, or per archive comment
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-reader\-workspace\-bytes\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum aggregate reader workspace per call (not process RAM)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-header\-count\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR
Maximum top\-level headers per physical archive parse
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-header\-bytes\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum plaintext header bytes per physical archive parse
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-scratch\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Directory for RAR5 filtered decoding above the buffering threshold
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-scratch\-bytes\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum temporary bytes for RAR5 scratch decoding
.TP
\fB\-\-rar50\-filter\-memory\-limit\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum workspace per RAR5 scratch filter
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-rar3\-vm\fR
Run RAR 3 VM filter programs other than the six standard ones. Off by default: they are arbitrary bytecode from the archive and can use a lot of CPU time. Enable only for archives you trust
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIARCHIVE\fR>
Archive path (first volume of a multi\-part set), optionally followed by sibling parts
